"""## Filtro 9: ELIMINACIÓN DE N-N-M SIN ARISTA PERPENDICULAR A 2 GUARDAS Y SIN OTRA ARISTA QUE SEA SEGMENTO DE GUARDA"""

# @title
# =========================================================
# FILTRO 9 — VALIDACIÓN DE N-N-M POR GUARDAS
# + VALIDACIÓN LATERAL DE PUNTOS N_pre
# + LIMPIEZA FINAL DE N-N-M CONFLICTIVOS POR MISMA BASE N-N
# =========================================================
#
# Objetivo general:
#   Depurar las superficies antes de la competencia final, dejando una capa
#   de triángulos más limpia y evitando que permanezcan N-N-M redundantes,
#   cruzados o solapados en planta XY.
#
#   Este filtro trabaja sobre la salida del Filtro 8 y aplica tres etapas
#   principales en este orden:
#
#   ETAPA 1 — Validación estructural de N-N-M por guardas
#   -----------------------------------------------------
#   Solo se evalúan los triángulos tipo N-N-M. Un N-N-M se conserva si cumple
#   simultáneamente estas dos condiciones:
#
#       1) Tiene una arista perpendicular en planta XY a 2 o más cables
#          de guarda.
#
#       2) Tiene otra arista distinta que corresponde a un segmento o
#          subsegmento de un cable de guarda.
#
#   Importante:
#       - La arista perpendicular y la arista segmento de guarda deben ser
#         diferentes.
#       - Si ambas condiciones ocurren sobre la misma arista, el N-N-M no se
#         considera estructuralmente válido.
#       - Los triángulos M-M-M, M-M-Q y M-M-N no se eliminan por esta etapa.
#
#
#   ETAPA 2 — Validación lateral de puntos N_pre
#   --------------------------------------------
#   Esta etapa se aplica a cualquier triángulo que contenga un punto N_pre,
#   sin importar si es N-N-M, M-M-N, M-M-Q u otro tipo.
#
#   Para cada N_pre activo se intenta identificar:
#
#       1) Su guarda/línea host, es decir, la línea de guarda donde cae o
#          desde la cual fue generado.
#
#       2) Uno o varios mástiles generadores/influenciadores válidos.
#
#   La guarda host define una recta orientada en planta XY. Cada generador
#   define un lado válido de esa recta mediante:
#
#       lado_valido_i = cross(v_guard, M_generador_i - N_pre)
#
#   Luego, para cada triángulo que contiene ese N_pre, se evalúa el lado del
#   centroide de los otros dos vértices:
#
#       lado_tri = cross(v_guard, centroide_otros_vertices - N_pre)
#
#   El triángulo se elimina solo si queda del lado contrario a TODOS los
#   generadores válidos del N_pre.
#
#   Esto permite casos como N_pre_03, donde un mismo punto puede estar
#   justificado por más de un mástil, por ejemplo M5 y M6. En ese caso basta
#   con que el triángulo quede del lado válido de uno de esos generadores.
#
#   Reglas de seguridad:
#       - Si no se puede identificar la guarda host de un N_pre, no se elimina.
#       - Si no se puede identificar ningún generador, no se elimina.
#       - Si el generador queda prácticamente sobre la línea host, no se elimina.
#       - Si el centroide evaluado cae prácticamente sobre la línea host,
#         se conserva por tolerancia.
#       - Si un triángulo tiene varios N_pre, debe cumplir la lateralidad de
#         todos los N_pre evaluables.
#
#
#   ETAPA 3 — Limpieza final de N-N-M por misma base N-N
#   ----------------------------------------------------
#   Esta es la etapa agregada en esta versión.
#
#   Problema que corrige:
#       Después de las etapas anteriores pueden quedar dos o más N-N-M que
#       comparten la misma arista N-N. Un caso típico es:
#
#           N_pre_01 - N_pre_03 - M1
#           N_pre_01 - N_pre_03 - M6
#
#       Estos triángulos NO son duplicados exactos, porque cambia el mástil.
#       Sin embargo, cuando ambos mástiles quedan del mismo lado de la base
#       N_pre_01 - N_pre_03 y las áreas proyectadas son muy parecidas, ambos
#       representan alternativas geométricas incompatibles para una zona
#       similar. Visualmente aparecen como N-N-M cruzados o solapados.
#
#   Procedimiento de esta etapa:
#       1) Se toman únicamente los N-N-M que sobrevivieron a las etapas 1 y 2.
#
#       2) Para cada N-N-M se identifica:
#
#             - su base N-N, por ejemplo (N_pre_01, N_pre_03);
#             - su vértice M, por ejemplo M1 o M6;
#             - el lado del M respecto a la línea N-N;
#             - el área proyectada en planta XY.
#
#       3) Se agrupan los N-N-M por:
#
#             - misma base N-N;
#             - mismo lado respecto a esa base.
#
#          Si dos N-N-M comparten base N-N pero están a lados opuestos de la
#          línea N-N, no se consideran conflicto automáticamente, porque
#          pueden representar superficies en regiones distintas.
#
#       4) Dentro de cada grupo se comparan pares de N-N-M. Dos N-N-M se
#          consideran conflictivos cuando:
#
#             - comparten la misma base N-N;
#             - el mástil de ambos está del mismo lado de esa base;
#             - sus áreas XY son iguales o muy parecidas; o presentan solape
#               XY significativo.
#
#       5) Para cada conjunto conflictivo se conserva solo un N-N-M.
#
#   Criterio para decidir cuál conservar:
#       Se usa un criterio determinístico y conservador:
#
#           a) Se prefiere el N-N-M que tenga más M-M-N complementarios
#              existentes. Esto ayuda a no dejar huecos en el relleno posterior.
#
#           b) Si empatan, se prefiere el que tenga más parejas válidas en la
#              validación estructural N-N-M.
#
#           c) Si todavía empatan, se conserva el que apareció primero en la
#              lista de entrada.
#
#   Qué NO hace esta etapa:
#       - No elimina N-N-M por el simple hecho de compartir una base N-N.
#       - No elimina N-N-M que estén a lados opuestos de la base N-N.
#       - No modifica M-M-M, M-M-Q ni M-M-N.
#       - No hace una competencia global de superficies; solo limpia conflictos
#         locales entre N-N-M con la misma base N-N.
#
#
# Contexto de entrada:
#   Este filtro recibe la salida del Filtro 8:
#
#       - kept_triangles_8 / filtered_triangles_final
#       - tri_nodes_after_filter_8 / filtered_tri_nodes_final
#       - filtered_results_final / results_input_8
#       - guard_wire_inputs
#       - masts
#       - S
#
#   En este punto pueden existir triángulos:
#
#       - M-M-M
#       - M-M-Q
#       - N-N-M
#       - M-M-N
#
#
# Salidas principales:
#   - kept_triangles_9
#   - kept_nnm_9
#   - removed_nnm_9
#   - removed_nnm_structural_9
#   - removed_nnm_same_nn_overlap_9
#   - removed_triangles_npre_lateral_9
#   - removed_triangles_nnm_guard_validation_9
#   - nnm_guard_validation_log_9
#   - npre_lateral_context_by_label_9
#   - npre_lateral_validation_log_9
#   - nnm_same_nn_overlap_cleanup_log_9
#   - guard_segments_filter_9
#   - tri_nodes_after_filter_9
#   - filtered_triangles_final
#   - filtered_tri_nodes_final
#   - filtered_results_final
#
# Visualización:
#   - Las aristas reales se agrupan por tipo.
#   - La leyenda interactiva controla las líneas reales.
#   - Todas las aristas de triángulos tienen grosor 3.
#
# Colores:
#   - MMM : gris
#   - MMQ : rojo
#   - NNM : verde
#   - MMN : morado
# =========================================================

import re
import numpy as np
import plotly.graph_objects as go
from collections import Counter


# =========================================================
# 0) PARÁMETROS
# =========================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------
# Parámetros del criterio N-N-M.
# ---------------------------------------------------------

# Tolerancia angular para considerar perpendicularidad.
# Se evalúa como |cos(theta)| <= PERP_DOT_TOL_9.
# 0.087 aprox equivale a ±5 grados alrededor de 90°.
PERP_DOT_TOL_9 = 0.087

# Tolerancias geométricas para detectar subsegmentos de guarda.
GUARD_SEGMENT_CROSS_TOL_9 = 1e-6
GUARD_SEGMENT_PARAM_TOL_9 = 1e-6
EDGE_MIN_LENGTH_XY_9 = 1e-9

# ---------------------------------------------------------
# Parámetros del criterio lateral N_pre.
# ---------------------------------------------------------

ENABLE_NPRE_LATERALITY_FILTER_9 = True

# Prefijos que identifican puntos N_pre.
NPRE_LABEL_PREFIXES_9 = ("N_pre", "N_PRE", "Npre", "NPRE")

# Tolerancia para decidir el lado de una recta host.
NPRE_LATERAL_SIDE_TOL_9 = 1e-7

# Criterio principal de eliminación lateral:
#   True  -> eliminar si el centroide de los otros vértices cae al lado inválido.
#   False -> no usar centroide para eliminar.
NPRE_REMOVE_IF_CENTROID_WRONG_SIDE_9 = True

# Criterio más agresivo:
#   True  -> eliminar si cualquier vértice relevante cae al lado inválido.
#   False -> no eliminar por un único vértice si el centroide no cae mal.
#
# Recomendado dejar False para no ser agresivo con tetras que cruzan cerca
# del límite o tienen un vértice sobre la línea host.
NPRE_REMOVE_IF_ANY_VERTEX_WRONG_SIDE_9 = False

# Si no se encuentra un campo explícito de mástil generador, se infiere
# buscando mástiles cuya arista M-N_pre sea perpendicular a 2 o más guardas.
NPRE_MIN_PERP_GUARDS_FOR_GENERATOR_9 = 2

# Si True, un campo explícito de generador en el nodo N_pre bloquea otros
# generadores inferidos. Recomendado False para permitir casos como N_pre_03,
# donde pueden existir dos direcciones válidas, por ejemplo M5 y M6.
NPRE_EXPLICIT_GENERATOR_IS_EXCLUSIVE_9 = False

# Si True, cuando varios mástiles cumplen la condición de perpendicularidad
# a 2 o más guardas, todos quedan como generadores/lados válidos.
NPRE_ALLOW_MULTIPLE_GENERATORS_9 = True

# Si no hay candidato perpendicular a 2 guardas, se permite usar el mástil
# no-host más cercano como generador inferido.
NPRE_ALLOW_NEAREST_MAST_FALLBACK_9 = True

# No se usan como generadores los mástiles que sean extremos de la guarda host.
NPRE_EXCLUDE_HOST_GUARD_ENDPOINTS_AS_GENERATOR_9 = True

# Si existe más de una guarda host candidata para un N_pre, se usa la que
# produzca mayor separación lateral con el mástil generador.
NPRE_CHOOSE_HOST_WITH_MAX_SIDE_MAGNITUDE_9 = True


# ---------------------------------------------------------
# Parámetros de limpieza final N-N-M por misma base N-N.
# ---------------------------------------------------------

# Activa/desactiva la limpieza final de N-N-M que comparten la misma base N-N.
ENABLE_NNM_SAME_NN_OVERLAP_CLEANUP_9 = True

# Tolerancia para decidir si el mástil M de un N-N-M está prácticamente
# sobre la línea N-N. Si queda sobre la línea, no se fuerza competencia.
NNM_SAME_NN_SIDE_TOL_9 = 1e-7

# Tolerancia relativa de área para considerar que dos N-N-M con la misma
# base N-N tienen áreas prácticamente iguales.
# 0.05 equivale a permitir hasta 5 % de diferencia relativa.
NNM_SAME_NN_AREA_REL_TOL_9 = 0.05

# Solape mínimo relativo para marcar conflicto aunque las áreas no sean
# exactamente iguales. Se calcula como:
#     area_intersección / min(area_1, area_2)
# Para el caso típico de dos N-N-M cruzados con la misma base, este valor
# suele ser significativo aunque las huellas no sean idénticas.
NNM_SAME_NN_MIN_OVERLAP_RATIO_9 = 0.20

# Si True, solo compiten N-N-M cuyo vértice M esté del mismo lado de la base N-N.
NNM_SAME_NN_REQUIRE_SAME_SIDE_9 = True

# Si True, se usa también el solape XY como evidencia de conflicto.
# Si False, la limpieza se apoya solo en igualdad/similitud de áreas.
NNM_SAME_NN_USE_OVERLAP_TEST_9 = True

# Tolerancia numérica para intersecciones de polígonos en XY.
NNM_SAME_NN_POLYGON_TOL_9 = 1e-9

# ---------------------------------------------------------
# Visualización.
# ---------------------------------------------------------

SHOW_REMOVED_NNM_9 = False
SHOW_REMOVED_NPRE_LATERAL_9 = False
SHOW_VALIDATION_SEGMENTS_9 = False
SHOW_NPRE_VALIDITY_ARROWS_9 = True

TRIANGLE_LINE_WIDTH_9 = 3
GUARD_LINE_WIDTH_9 = 3
MAST_LINE_WIDTH_9 = 8
VALIDATION_SEGMENT_WIDTH_9 = 6


# =========================================================
# 1) UTILIDADES M/N/Q Y TIPOS
# =========================================================

def node_family_filter_9(node):
    """
    Normaliza tipos de nodo.

    Compatibilidad:
      - "M" o "mast_top" -> M
      - "N"              -> N
      - "Q"              -> Q
    """
    raw_type = str(node.get("type", "")).strip()
    label = str(node.get("label", "")).strip()

    if raw_type in ["M", "mast_top", "mast"] or label.startswith("M"):
        return "M"

    if raw_type == "N" or raw_type.startswith("auxiliary_N") or label.startswith("N"):
        return "N"

    if raw_type == "Q" or label.startswith("Q"):
        return "Q"

    return raw_type


def normalize_triangle_type_filter_9(tri_type):
    """
    Normaliza tipos compactos y tipos con guiones.
    """
    if tri_type is None:
        return None

    mapping = {
        "MMM": "M-M-M",
        "MMQ": "M-M-Q",
        "NNM": "N-N-M",
        "MMN": "M-M-N",
        "MQQ": "M-Q-Q",
        "QQQ": "Q-Q-Q",
        "MNQ": "M-N-Q",
        "NNN": "N-N-N",
        "NNQ": "N-N-Q",
    }

    tri_type = str(tri_type).strip()
    return mapping.get(tri_type, tri_type)


def compact_triangle_type_filter_9(tri_type):
    """
    Convierte tipo con guiones a código compacto.
    """
    tri_type = normalize_triangle_type_filter_9(tri_type)

    mapping = {
        "M-M-M": "MMM",
        "M-M-Q": "MMQ",
        "N-N-M": "NNM",
        "M-M-N": "MMN",
        "M-Q-Q": "MQQ",
        "Q-Q-Q": "QQQ",
        "M-N-Q": "MNQ",
        "N-N-N": "NNN",
        "N-N-Q": "NNQ",
    }

    return mapping.get(tri_type, tri_type)


def classify_triangle_type_filter_9(tri_data):
    """
    Clasifica triángulos usando familias M/N/Q.
    """
    families = [
        node_family_filter_9(n)
        for n in tri_data["nodes"]
    ]

    nM = families.count("M")
    nN = families.count("N")
    nQ = families.count("Q")

    if nM == 3:
        return "M-M-M"

    if nM == 2 and nQ == 1:
        return "M-M-Q"

    if nN == 2 and nM == 1:
        return "N-N-M"

    if nM == 2 and nN == 1:
        return "M-M-N"

    if nM == 1 and nQ == 2:
        return "M-Q-Q"

    if nQ == 3:
        return "Q-Q-Q"

    if nM == 1 and nN == 1 and nQ == 1:
        return "M-N-Q"

    if nN == 3:
        return "N-N-N"

    if nN == 2 and nQ == 1:
        return "N-N-Q"

    return "UNKNOWN"


def decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri):
    """
    Asegura que cada triángulo tenga:
      - triangle_type: tipo con guiones.
      - type: código compacto.
    """
    tri_ext = dict(tri)

    raw_type = tri_ext.get("triangle_type", tri_ext.get("type", None))
    tri_type = normalize_triangle_type_filter_9(raw_type)

    if tri_type is None or tri_type == "UNKNOWN":
        tri_type = classify_triangle_type_filter_9(tri_ext)

    tri_ext["triangle_type"] = tri_type
    tri_ext["type"] = compact_triangle_type_filter_9(tri_type)

    return tri_ext


def format_labels_filter_9(labels):
    """
    Convierte labels tipo tuple/list/string a texto legible.
    """
    if isinstance(labels, (tuple, list)):
        return "-".join(str(x) for x in labels)

    return str(labels)


def triangle_labels_filter_9(tri_data):
    """
    Devuelve labels robustos para triángulos.
    """
    if "labels" in tri_data:
        return tri_data["labels"]

    return tuple(
        str(n.get("label", ""))
        for n in tri_data.get("nodes", [])
    )


def get_result_by_mast_filter_9(results_obj, mast_idx):
    return results_obj[mast_idx]


def edge_label_key_filter_9(a_label, b_label):
    """
    Llave no orientada para aristas por etiqueta.
    """
    return tuple(sorted([str(a_label), str(b_label)]))


def node_xyz_filter_9(node):
    return np.array([
        float(node["x"]),
        float(node["y"]),
        float(node["z"]),
    ], dtype=float)


def node_xy_filter_9(node):
    return np.array([
        float(node["x"]),
        float(node["y"]),
    ], dtype=float)


def is_npre_node_filter_9(node):
    """
    Detecta puntos N_pre por etiqueta o por metadatos.
    """
    label = str(node.get("label", "")).strip()
    raw_type = str(node.get("type", "")).strip()

    if any(label.startswith(prefix) for prefix in NPRE_LABEL_PREFIXES_9):
        return True

    if "pre" in label.lower() and node_family_filter_9(node) == "N":
        return True

    if "pre" in raw_type.lower() and node_family_filter_9(node) == "N":
        return True

    return False


# =========================================================
# 2) GUARDAS COMO SEGMENTOS DE REFERENCIA
# =========================================================

def guard_wire_segments_from_inputs_filter_9(masts, guard_wire_inputs=None):
    """
    Construye segmentos de guarda originales desde guard_wire_inputs.
    """
    segments = []

    if guard_wire_inputs is None:
        return segments

    for k, gw in enumerate(guard_wire_inputs):

        if isinstance(gw, dict):
            i = int(gw["i"])
            j = int(gw["j"])
        else:
            i = int(gw[0])
            j = int(gw[1])

        mi = masts[i]
        mj = masts[j]

        p1 = np.array([mi.x, mi.y, mi.h], dtype=float)
        p2 = np.array([mj.x, mj.y, mj.h], dtype=float)

        v_xy = p2[:2] - p1[:2]
        length_xy = float(np.linalg.norm(v_xy))

        segments.append({
            "guard_idx": k,
            "mast_i": i,
            "mast_j": j,
            "label_a": f"M{i}",
            "label_b": f"M{j}",
            "labels": (f"M{i}", f"M{j}"),
            "p1": p1,
            "p2": p2,
            "p1_xy": p1[:2],
            "p2_xy": p2[:2],
            "v_xy": v_xy,
            "length_xy": length_xy,
        })

    return segments


# =========================================================
# 3) UTILIDADES GEOMÉTRICAS PARA ARISTAS Y GUARDAS
# =========================================================

def cross2d_filter_9(a, b):
    return float(a[0] * b[1] - a[1] * b[0])


def edge_xy_data_filter_9(edge_a, edge_b):
    """
    Devuelve datos XY básicos de una arista.
    """
    a_xy = np.array([edge_a["x"], edge_a["y"]], dtype=float)
    b_xy = np.array([edge_b["x"], edge_b["y"]], dtype=float)
    v_xy = b_xy - a_xy
    length_xy = float(np.linalg.norm(v_xy))

    return a_xy, b_xy, v_xy, length_xy


def triangle_edges_filter_9(tri_data):
    """
    Devuelve las tres aristas de un triángulo.
    """
    tri_ext = decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri_data)
    n1, n2, n3 = tri_ext["nodes"]

    return [
        (n1, n2),
        (n2, n3),
        (n3, n1),
    ]


def edge_is_perpendicular_to_guard_filter_9(
    edge_a,
    edge_b,
    guard,
    dot_tol=0.087,
    min_length=1e-9
):
    """
    Evalúa si una arista es perpendicular a una guarda en planta XY.

    Usa producto punto normalizado:

        |dot(u_edge, u_guard)| <= dot_tol
    """
    _, _, v_edge, len_edge = edge_xy_data_filter_9(edge_a, edge_b)
    v_guard = np.asarray(guard["v_xy"], dtype=float)
    len_guard = float(guard.get("length_xy", np.linalg.norm(v_guard)))

    if len_edge <= min_length or len_guard <= min_length:
        return False, None

    u_edge = v_edge / len_edge
    u_guard = v_guard / len_guard

    dot_abs = abs(float(np.dot(u_edge, u_guard)))

    is_perp = dot_abs <= dot_tol

    return is_perp, {
        "guard_idx": guard["guard_idx"],
        "guard_labels": guard["labels"],
        "dot_abs": dot_abs,
    }


def edge_perpendicular_to_two_guards_filter_9(
    edge_a,
    edge_b,
    guard_segments,
    dot_tol=0.087,
    min_length=1e-9
):
    """
    Retorna True si la arista es perpendicular a 2 o más guardas.
    """
    perp_records = []

    for guard in guard_segments:
        is_perp, info = edge_is_perpendicular_to_guard_filter_9(
            edge_a=edge_a,
            edge_b=edge_b,
            guard=guard,
            dot_tol=dot_tol,
            min_length=min_length
        )

        if is_perp:
            perp_records.append(info)

    return len(perp_records) >= 2, perp_records


def point_projection_param_on_segment_filter_9(p_xy, a_xy, b_xy):
    """
    Parámetro t de la proyección de p sobre AB en XY.
    """
    ab = b_xy - a_xy
    den = float(np.dot(ab, ab))

    if den <= 1e-15:
        return None

    return float(np.dot(p_xy - a_xy, ab) / den)


def point_on_guard_segment_xy_filter_9(
    p_xy,
    guard,
    cross_tol=1e-6,
    param_tol=1e-6
):
    """
    Verifica si un punto XY está sobre el segmento de una guarda.
    """
    a = np.asarray(guard["p1_xy"], dtype=float)
    b = np.asarray(guard["p2_xy"], dtype=float)
    v = b - a
    length = float(np.linalg.norm(v))

    if length <= EDGE_MIN_LENGTH_XY_9:
        return False, None

    p = np.asarray(p_xy, dtype=float)
    ap = p - a

    # Distancia perpendicular aproximada usando área / longitud.
    dist_line = abs(cross2d_filter_9(v, ap)) / length

    if dist_line > cross_tol:
        return False, None

    t = point_projection_param_on_segment_filter_9(p, a, b)

    if t is None:
        return False, None

    if not (-param_tol <= t <= 1.0 + param_tol):
        return False, None

    return True, float(t)


def edge_is_guard_subsegment_filter_9(
    edge_a,
    edge_b,
    guard,
    cross_tol=1e-6,
    param_tol=1e-6,
    min_length=1e-9
):
    """
    Verifica si la arista AB es un segmento o subsegmento de una guarda.

    Para ser subsegmento de guarda:
      - A y B deben estar sobre la misma guarda.
      - Ambos puntos deben estar dentro de los límites de la guarda.
      - La arista debe tener longitud no nula en XY.
    """
    a_xy, b_xy, _, len_edge = edge_xy_data_filter_9(edge_a, edge_b)

    if len_edge <= min_length:
        return False, None

    a_on, t_a = point_on_guard_segment_xy_filter_9(
        p_xy=a_xy,
        guard=guard,
        cross_tol=cross_tol,
        param_tol=param_tol
    )

    if not a_on:
        return False, None

    b_on, t_b = point_on_guard_segment_xy_filter_9(
        p_xy=b_xy,
        guard=guard,
        cross_tol=cross_tol,
        param_tol=param_tol
    )

    if not b_on:
        return False, None

    if abs(t_a - t_b) <= param_tol:
        return False, None

    return True, {
        "guard_idx": guard["guard_idx"],
        "guard_labels": guard["labels"],
        "t_a": float(t_a),
        "t_b": float(t_b),
    }


def edge_as_guard_segment_filter_9(
    edge_a,
    edge_b,
    guard_segments,
    cross_tol=1e-6,
    param_tol=1e-6,
    min_length=1e-9
):
    """
    Retorna True si la arista es subsegmento de al menos una guarda.
    """
    guard_records = []

    for guard in guard_segments:
        is_segment, info = edge_is_guard_subsegment_filter_9(
            edge_a=edge_a,
            edge_b=edge_b,
            guard=guard,
            cross_tol=cross_tol,
            param_tol=param_tol,
            min_length=min_length
        )

        if is_segment:
            guard_records.append(info)

    return len(guard_records) > 0, guard_records


# =========================================================
# 4) CRITERIO ESTRUCTURAL N-N-M
# =========================================================

def evaluate_nnm_guard_conditions_filter_9(
    tri_data,
    guard_segments,
    perp_dot_tol=0.087,
    cross_tol=1e-6,
    param_tol=1e-6,
    min_length=1e-9
):
    """
    Evalúa las dos condiciones para un N-N-M:

      1) Una arista perpendicular a 2 guardas.
      2) Otra arista distinta que sea segmento de guarda.
    """
    tri_ext = decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri_data)
    edges = triangle_edges_filter_9(tri_ext)

    edge_reports = []
    perp_edge_indices = []
    guard_segment_edge_indices = []

    for edge_idx, (na, nb) in enumerate(edges):
        edge_labels = (
            str(na.get("label", "")),
            str(nb.get("label", ""))
        )

        is_perp_two, perp_records = edge_perpendicular_to_two_guards_filter_9(
            edge_a=na,
            edge_b=nb,
            guard_segments=guard_segments,
            dot_tol=perp_dot_tol,
            min_length=min_length
        )

        is_guard_segment, guard_records = edge_as_guard_segment_filter_9(
            edge_a=na,
            edge_b=nb,
            guard_segments=guard_segments,
            cross_tol=cross_tol,
            param_tol=param_tol,
            min_length=min_length
        )

        if is_perp_two:
            perp_edge_indices.append(edge_idx)

        if is_guard_segment:
            guard_segment_edge_indices.append(edge_idx)

        edge_reports.append({
            "edge_idx": edge_idx,
            "edge_labels": edge_labels,
            "is_perpendicular_to_two_guards": bool(is_perp_two),
            "perpendicular_guard_count": len(perp_records),
            "perpendicular_guard_records": perp_records,
            "is_guard_segment": bool(is_guard_segment),
            "guard_segment_records": guard_records,
        })

    valid_pairs = []

    for perp_idx in perp_edge_indices:
        for guard_idx in guard_segment_edge_indices:
            if perp_idx == guard_idx:
                continue

            valid_pairs.append({
                "perpendicular_edge_idx": perp_idx,
                "guard_segment_edge_idx": guard_idx,
                "perpendicular_edge_labels": edge_reports[perp_idx]["edge_labels"],
                "guard_segment_edge_labels": edge_reports[guard_idx]["edge_labels"],
            })

    is_valid = len(valid_pairs) > 0

    return {
        "triangle_labels": triangle_labels_filter_9(tri_ext),
        "triangle_type": tri_ext["triangle_type"],
        "is_valid_nnm": bool(is_valid),
        "perp_edge_indices": perp_edge_indices,
        "guard_segment_edge_indices": guard_segment_edge_indices,
        "valid_pairs": valid_pairs,
        "edge_reports": edge_reports,
    }


# =========================================================
# 5) CONTEXTO DE LATERALIDAD PARA N_pre
# =========================================================

def collect_node_by_label_filter_9(tri_nodes, triangles=None, masts=None):
    """
    Construye diccionario label -> nodo.
    Incluye nodos de tri_nodes, triángulos y mástiles.
    """
    node_by_label = {}

    if tri_nodes is not None:
        for n in tri_nodes:
            if isinstance(n, dict) and "label" in n:
                node_by_label[str(n["label"])] = n

    if triangles is not None:
        for tri in triangles:
            for n in tri.get("nodes", []):
                if isinstance(n, dict) and "label" in n:
                    node_by_label[str(n["label"])] = n

    if masts is not None:
        for i, mast in enumerate(masts):
            label = f"M{i}"
            if label not in node_by_label:
                node_by_label[label] = {
                    "label": label,
                    "type": "mast_top",
                    "x": float(mast.x),
                    "y": float(mast.y),
                    "z": float(mast.h),
                }

    return node_by_label


def parse_guard_labels_from_value_filter_9(value):
    """
    Intenta extraer una pareja de labels M* desde un campo de metadatos.
    Acepta:
      - ("M1", "M2")
      - ["M1", "M2"]
      - {"label_a": "M1", "label_b": "M2"}
      - {"i": 1, "j": 2}
      - "M1-M2"
      - "('M1', 'M2')"
    """
    if value is None:
        return None

    if isinstance(value, dict):
        if "label_a" in value and "label_b" in value:
            return edge_label_key_filter_9(value["label_a"], value["label_b"])

        if "labels" in value:
            return parse_guard_labels_from_value_filter_9(value["labels"])

        if "i" in value and "j" in value:
            return edge_label_key_filter_9(f"M{int(value['i'])}", f"M{int(value['j'])}")

        if "mast_i" in value and "mast_j" in value:
            return edge_label_key_filter_9(f"M{int(value['mast_i'])}", f"M{int(value['mast_j'])}")

    if isinstance(value, (tuple, list)) and len(value) == 2:
        a, b = value

        if isinstance(a, int) and isinstance(b, int):
            return edge_label_key_filter_9(f"M{a}", f"M{b}")

        return edge_label_key_filter_9(str(a), str(b))

    if isinstance(value, str):
        labels = re.findall(r"M\d+", value)

        if len(labels) >= 2:
            return edge_label_key_filter_9(labels[0], labels[1])

    return None


def parse_mast_label_from_value_filter_9(value):
    """
    Intenta extraer un label de mástil desde un campo de metadatos.
    """
    if value is None:
        return None

    if isinstance(value, dict):
        for key in [
            "label",
            "mast_label",
            "source_mast",
            "generator_mast",
            "influence_mast",
            "owner_mast",
            "ref_mast",
            "m_label",
        ]:
            if key in value:
                out = parse_mast_label_from_value_filter_9(value[key])
                if out is not None:
                    return out

        for key in ["i", "mast_i", "idx", "mast_idx"]:
            if key in value:
                try:
                    return f"M{int(value[key])}"
                except Exception:
                    pass

    if isinstance(value, int):
        return f"M{value}"

    if isinstance(value, str):
        m = re.search(r"M\d+", value)
        if m:
            return m.group(0)

        if value.strip().isdigit():
            return f"M{int(value.strip())}"

    return None


def get_explicit_host_guard_labels_from_npre_filter_9(n_node):
    """
    Busca en los metadatos del nodo una guarda host explícita.
    """
    field_candidates = [
        "host_guard",
        "guard",
        "guard_edge",
        "parent_guard",
        "source_guard",
        "wire",
        "guard_wire",
        "guard_labels",
        "host_edge",
        "edge",
    ]

    for key in field_candidates:
        if key in n_node:
            parsed = parse_guard_labels_from_value_filter_9(n_node.get(key))
            if parsed is not None:
                return parsed

    info = n_node.get("info", None)

    if isinstance(info, dict):
        for key in field_candidates:
            if key in info:
                parsed = parse_guard_labels_from_value_filter_9(info.get(key))
                if parsed is not None:
                    return parsed

    return None


def get_explicit_generator_label_from_npre_filter_9(n_node):
    """
    Busca en los metadatos del nodo un mástil generador explícito.
    """
    field_candidates = [
        "generator_mast",
        "source_mast",
        "influence_mast",
        "influencing_mast",
        "owner_mast",
        "ref_mast",
        "parent_mast",
        "support_mast",
        "created_by_mast",
        "generated_by",
        "mast_label",
        "m_label",
        "mast_idx",
        "source_mast_idx",
        "generator_mast_idx",
    ]

    for key in field_candidates:
        if key in n_node:
            parsed = parse_mast_label_from_value_filter_9(n_node.get(key))
            if parsed is not None:
                return parsed

    info = n_node.get("info", None)

    if isinstance(info, dict):
        for key in field_candidates:
            if key in info:
                parsed = parse_mast_label_from_value_filter_9(info.get(key))
                if parsed is not None:
                    return parsed

    return None


def guard_segment_by_labels_filter_9(guard_segments, labels_key):
    """
    Busca un segmento de guarda por llave de labels.
    """
    if labels_key is None:
        return None

    labels_key = edge_label_key_filter_9(labels_key[0], labels_key[1])

    for guard in guard_segments:
        if edge_label_key_filter_9(*guard["labels"]) == labels_key:
            return guard

    return None


def find_host_guard_candidates_for_npre_filter_9(
    n_node,
    guard_segments,
    cross_tol=1e-6,
    param_tol=1e-6
):
    """
    Encuentra guardas host candidatas para un punto N_pre.
    Primero intenta metadatos explícitos; si no existen, usa geometría.
    """
    candidates = []
    n_xy = node_xy_filter_9(n_node)

    explicit_labels = get_explicit_host_guard_labels_from_npre_filter_9(n_node)

    if explicit_labels is not None:
        guard = guard_segment_by_labels_filter_9(
            guard_segments=guard_segments,
            labels_key=explicit_labels
        )

        if guard is not None:
            on_seg, t_val = point_on_guard_segment_xy_filter_9(
                p_xy=n_xy,
                guard=guard,
                cross_tol=max(cross_tol, 1e-5),
                param_tol=max(param_tol, 1e-5)
            )

            candidates.append({
                "guard": guard,
                "t": t_val,
                "source": "explicit_metadata",
                "point_on_segment": bool(on_seg),
            })

            return candidates

    for guard in guard_segments:
        on_seg, t_val = point_on_guard_segment_xy_filter_9(
            p_xy=n_xy,
            guard=guard,
            cross_tol=cross_tol,
            param_tol=param_tol
        )

        if on_seg:
            candidates.append({
                "guard": guard,
                "t": t_val,
                "source": "geometry_point_on_guard",
                "point_on_segment": True,
            })

    return candidates


def infer_generator_mast_for_npre_filter_9(
    n_node,
    mast_nodes,
    guard_segments,
    host_guard=None,
    perp_dot_tol=0.087,
    min_length=1e-9
):
    """
    Identifica el mástil generador/influenciador de un N_pre.

    Prioridad:
      1) Metadatos explícitos del nodo.
      2) Mástil no-host cuya arista M-N_pre sea perpendicular a 2 o más guardas.
      3) Fallback: mástil no-host más cercano.
    """
    explicit_label = get_explicit_generator_label_from_npre_filter_9(n_node)

    if explicit_label is not None and explicit_label in mast_nodes:
        return {
            "generator_node": mast_nodes[explicit_label],
            "generator_label": explicit_label,
            "source": "explicit_metadata",
            "perpendicular_guard_count": None,
            "perpendicular_guard_records": [],
            "distance_xy": float(np.linalg.norm(
                node_xy_filter_9(mast_nodes[explicit_label]) - node_xy_filter_9(n_node)
            )),
        }

    host_labels = set()

    if host_guard is not None:
        host_labels = set(host_guard.get("labels", []))

    candidates = []

    for m_label, m_node in mast_nodes.items():

        if (
            NPRE_EXCLUDE_HOST_GUARD_ENDPOINTS_AS_GENERATOR_9
            and m_label in host_labels
        ):
            continue

        is_perp_two, perp_records = edge_perpendicular_to_two_guards_filter_9(
            edge_a=n_node,
            edge_b=m_node,
            guard_segments=guard_segments,
            dot_tol=perp_dot_tol,
            min_length=min_length
        )

        dist_xy = float(np.linalg.norm(
            node_xy_filter_9(m_node) - node_xy_filter_9(n_node)
        ))

        candidates.append({
            "generator_node": m_node,
            "generator_label": m_label,
            "source": "inferred_perpendicular_to_two_guards" if is_perp_two else "candidate_nearest",
            "perpendicular_guard_count": len(perp_records),
            "perpendicular_guard_records": perp_records,
            "distance_xy": dist_xy,
            "is_perp_two": bool(is_perp_two),
        })

    perp_candidates = [
        c for c in candidates
        if c["perpendicular_guard_count"] >= NPRE_MIN_PERP_GUARDS_FOR_GENERATOR_9
    ]

    if perp_candidates:
        # Preferir mayor número de guardas perpendiculares y luego menor distancia.
        perp_candidates.sort(
            key=lambda c: (
                -c["perpendicular_guard_count"],
                c["distance_xy"]
            )
        )
        return perp_candidates[0]

    if NPRE_ALLOW_NEAREST_MAST_FALLBACK_9 and candidates:
        candidates.sort(key=lambda c: c["distance_xy"])
        out = candidates[0]
        out = dict(out)
        out["source"] = "fallback_nearest_non_host_mast"
        return out

    return None




def infer_generator_masts_for_npre_filter_9(
    n_node,
    mast_nodes,
    guard_segments,
    host_guard=None,
    perp_dot_tol=0.087,
    min_length=1e-9
):
    """
    Identifica uno o varios mástiles generadores/influenciadores de un N_pre.

    Prioridad:
      1) Metadatos explícitos del nodo.
      2) Todos los mástiles no-host cuya arista M-N_pre sea perpendicular
         a 2 o más guardas.
      3) Fallback: mástil no-host más cercano, solo si no hay candidatos
         por perpendicularidad.

    Esta función corrige el caso en el que un N_pre tiene dos direcciones
    válidas, por ejemplo N_pre_03 con influencia desde M5 y M6.
    """
    explicit_label = get_explicit_generator_label_from_npre_filter_9(n_node)

    host_labels = set()

    if host_guard is not None:
        host_labels = set(host_guard.get("labels", []))

    candidates = []

    for m_label, m_node in mast_nodes.items():

        if (
            NPRE_EXCLUDE_HOST_GUARD_ENDPOINTS_AS_GENERATOR_9
            and m_label in host_labels
            and m_label != explicit_label
        ):
            continue

        is_perp_two, perp_records = edge_perpendicular_to_two_guards_filter_9(
            edge_a=n_node,
            edge_b=m_node,
            guard_segments=guard_segments,
            dot_tol=perp_dot_tol,
            min_length=min_length
        )

        dist_xy = float(np.linalg.norm(
            node_xy_filter_9(m_node) - node_xy_filter_9(n_node)
        ))

        is_explicit = bool(explicit_label is not None and m_label == explicit_label)

        if is_explicit:
            source = "explicit_metadata"
        elif is_perp_two:
            source = "inferred_perpendicular_to_two_guards"
        else:
            source = "candidate_nearest"

        candidates.append({
            "generator_node": m_node,
            "generator_label": m_label,
            "source": source,
            "is_explicit": is_explicit,
            "perpendicular_guard_count": len(perp_records),
            "perpendicular_guard_records": perp_records,
            "distance_xy": dist_xy,
            "is_perp_two": bool(is_perp_two),
        })

    explicit_candidates = [
        c for c in candidates
        if c.get("is_explicit", False)
    ]

    if explicit_candidates and NPRE_EXPLICIT_GENERATOR_IS_EXCLUSIVE_9:
        explicit_candidates.sort(key=lambda c: c["distance_xy"])
        return explicit_candidates[:1]

    perp_candidates = [
        c for c in candidates
        if c["perpendicular_guard_count"] >= NPRE_MIN_PERP_GUARDS_FOR_GENERATOR_9
    ]

    selected = []
    seen_labels = set()

    # Mantener explícitos primero si existen, pero permitir otros generadores
    # cuando NPRE_EXPLICIT_GENERATOR_IS_EXCLUSIVE_9 = False.
    for c in explicit_candidates:
        if c["generator_label"] not in seen_labels:
            selected.append(c)
            seen_labels.add(c["generator_label"])

    if perp_candidates:
        perp_candidates.sort(
            key=lambda c: (
                -c["perpendicular_guard_count"],
                c["distance_xy"],
                c["generator_label"]
            )
        )

        if NPRE_ALLOW_MULTIPLE_GENERATORS_9:
            for c in perp_candidates:
                if c["generator_label"] not in seen_labels:
                    selected.append(c)
                    seen_labels.add(c["generator_label"])
        else:
            c = perp_candidates[0]
            if c["generator_label"] not in seen_labels:
                selected.append(c)
                seen_labels.add(c["generator_label"])

    if selected:
        selected.sort(
            key=lambda c: (
                0 if c.get("is_explicit", False) else 1,
                -c["perpendicular_guard_count"],
                c["distance_xy"],
                c["generator_label"]
            )
        )
        return selected

    if NPRE_ALLOW_NEAREST_MAST_FALLBACK_9 and candidates:
        candidates.sort(key=lambda c: c["distance_xy"])
        out = dict(candidates[0])
        out["source"] = "fallback_nearest_non_host_mast"
        return [out]

    return []


def build_valid_side_records_for_npre_filter_9(
    n_node,
    host_guard,
    generator_records,
    side_tol=1e-7
):
    """
    Construye lados válidos para un N_pre a partir de una host y uno o más
    generadores. Cada generador aporta un semiplano válido.
    """
    n_xy = node_xy_filter_9(n_node)
    v_guard = np.asarray(host_guard["v_xy"], dtype=float)

    side_records = []

    for gen in generator_records:
        generator_node = gen["generator_node"]
        g_xy = node_xy_filter_9(generator_node)
        side_valid = cross2d_filter_9(v_guard, g_xy - n_xy)

        if abs(side_valid) <= side_tol:
            continue

        rec = {
            **gen,
            "side_valid": float(side_valid),
            "side_sign": 1 if side_valid > 0 else -1,
            "side_abs": abs(float(side_valid)),
        }

        side_records.append(rec)

    side_records.sort(
        key=lambda c: (
            0 if c.get("is_explicit", False) else 1,
            -c.get("perpendicular_guard_count", 0),
            -c.get("side_abs", 0.0),
            c.get("distance_xy", 1e18),
            c.get("generator_label", "")
        )
    )

    return side_records


def choose_best_host_guard_with_generators_for_npre_filter_9(
    n_node,
    host_candidates,
    mast_nodes,
    guard_segments
):
    """
    Evalúa todas las guardas host candidatas y escoge la que permite más
    generadores/lados válidos.
    """
    scored_hosts = []

    for cand in host_candidates:
        guard = cand["guard"]

        generator_records = infer_generator_masts_for_npre_filter_9(
            n_node=n_node,
            mast_nodes=mast_nodes,
            guard_segments=guard_segments,
            host_guard=guard,
            perp_dot_tol=PERP_DOT_TOL_9,
            min_length=EDGE_MIN_LENGTH_XY_9
        )

        valid_side_records = build_valid_side_records_for_npre_filter_9(
            n_node=n_node,
            host_guard=guard,
            generator_records=generator_records,
            side_tol=NPRE_LATERAL_SIDE_TOL_9
        )

        unique_side_signs = sorted({
            int(rec["side_sign"])
            for rec in valid_side_records
        })

        score = (
            len(valid_side_records),
            len(unique_side_signs),
            max([rec.get("side_abs", 0.0) for rec in valid_side_records] or [0.0]),
            sum([rec.get("side_abs", 0.0) for rec in valid_side_records]),
            1 if cand.get("point_on_segment", False) else 0,
        )

        scored_hosts.append({
            **cand,
            "generator_records": generator_records,
            "valid_side_records": valid_side_records,
            "unique_side_signs": unique_side_signs,
            "host_score": score,
        })

    if not scored_hosts:
        return None

    scored_hosts.sort(
        key=lambda c: c["host_score"],
        reverse=True
    )

    return scored_hosts[0]

def build_mast_nodes_dict_filter_9(tri_nodes, triangles, masts):
    """
    Construye diccionario de mástiles por label.
    """
    node_by_label = collect_node_by_label_filter_9(
        tri_nodes=tri_nodes,
        triangles=triangles,
        masts=masts
    )

    mast_nodes = {
        label: node
        for label, node in node_by_label.items()
        if node_family_filter_9(node) == "M"
    }

    return mast_nodes


def choose_best_host_guard_for_npre_filter_9(
    n_node,
    host_candidates,
    generator_node
):
    """
    Si hay varias guardas host, elige la que define mejor la lateralidad
    con el generador.
    """
    if not host_candidates:
        return None

    if generator_node is None:
        return host_candidates[0]

    n_xy = node_xy_filter_9(n_node)
    g_xy = node_xy_filter_9(generator_node)

    scored = []

    for cand in host_candidates:
        guard = cand["guard"]
        v = np.asarray(guard["v_xy"], dtype=float)

        side = cross2d_filter_9(v, g_xy - n_xy)
        scored.append({
            **cand,
            "side_value": float(side),
            "side_abs": abs(float(side)),
        })

    if NPRE_CHOOSE_HOST_WITH_MAX_SIDE_MAGNITUDE_9:
        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c["side_abs"], reverse=True)
    else:
        scored.sort(key=lambda c: 0)

    return scored[0]


def build_npre_lateral_context_filter_9(
    tri_nodes,
    triangles,
    masts,
    guard_segments
):
    """
    Construye contexto de lateralidad para todos los N_pre activos.

    Versión corregida:
      - Un N_pre puede tener uno o varios generadores válidos.
      - Cada generador define un lado válido.
      - Un triángulo se conserva si cae en el lado válido de al menos uno
        de esos generadores.
    """
    node_by_label = collect_node_by_label_filter_9(
        tri_nodes=tri_nodes,
        triangles=triangles,
        masts=masts
    )

    mast_nodes = build_mast_nodes_dict_filter_9(
        tri_nodes=tri_nodes,
        triangles=triangles,
        masts=masts
    )

    npre_nodes = {
        label: node
        for label, node in node_by_label.items()
        if is_npre_node_filter_9(node)
    }

    context_by_label = {}

    for n_label, n_node in npre_nodes.items():
        host_candidates = find_host_guard_candidates_for_npre_filter_9(
            n_node=n_node,
            guard_segments=guard_segments,
            cross_tol=GUARD_SEGMENT_CROSS_TOL_9,
            param_tol=GUARD_SEGMENT_PARAM_TOL_9
        )

        if not host_candidates:
            context_by_label[n_label] = {
                "n_label": n_label,
                "n_node": n_node,
                "status": "no_host_guard_found_keep_by_safety",
                "can_apply": False,
                "reason": "No se pudo identificar guarda/línea host para este N_pre.",
            }
            continue

        best_host = choose_best_host_guard_with_generators_for_npre_filter_9(
            n_node=n_node,
            host_candidates=host_candidates,
            mast_nodes=mast_nodes,
            guard_segments=guard_segments
        )

        if best_host is None:
            context_by_label[n_label] = {
                "n_label": n_label,
                "n_node": n_node,
                "status": "no_best_host_guard_keep_by_safety",
                "can_apply": False,
                "reason": "No se pudo seleccionar guarda host.",
                "host_candidates": host_candidates,
            }
            continue

        guard = best_host["guard"]
        generator_records = best_host.get("generator_records", [])
        valid_side_records = best_host.get("valid_side_records", [])

        if not generator_records:
            context_by_label[n_label] = {
                "n_label": n_label,
                "n_node": n_node,
                "status": "no_generator_mast_found_keep_by_safety",
                "can_apply": False,
                "reason": "No se pudo identificar ningún mástil generador/influenciador para este N_pre.",
                "host_guard": guard,
                "host_source": best_host.get("source"),
                "host_candidates": host_candidates,
            }
            continue

        if not valid_side_records:
            context_by_label[n_label] = {
                "n_label": n_label,
                "n_node": n_node,
                "status": "all_generators_on_host_line_keep_by_safety",
                "can_apply": False,
                "reason": "Los generadores detectados quedan prácticamente sobre la línea host.",
                "host_guard": guard,
                "host_source": best_host.get("source"),
                "host_t": best_host.get("t"),
                "generator_records": generator_records,
                "generator_labels": [rec["generator_label"] for rec in generator_records],
            }
            continue

        first = valid_side_records[0]

        context_by_label[n_label] = {
            "n_label": n_label,
            "n_node": n_node,
            "status": "ok",
            "can_apply": True,
            "reason": "Lateralidad aplicable con uno o varios generadores válidos.",
            "host_guard": guard,
            "host_source": best_host.get("source"),
            "host_t": best_host.get("t"),
            "host_score": best_host.get("host_score"),
            "generator_records": generator_records,
            "valid_side_records": valid_side_records,
            "generator_labels": [rec["generator_label"] for rec in valid_side_records],
            "valid_side_signs": sorted({int(rec["side_sign"]) for rec in valid_side_records}),
            "multi_generator": len(valid_side_records) > 1,

            # Campos de compatibilidad con la versión anterior.
            "generator": first,
            "generator_label": first["generator_label"],
            "generator_node": first["generator_node"],
            "side_valid": float(first["side_valid"]),
            "side_sign": int(first["side_sign"]),
        }

    return context_by_label



def relevant_test_points_for_npre_triangle_filter_9(tri, npre_node, host_guard):
    """
    Define puntos de prueba para lateralidad:
      - centroide de los otros dos vértices;
      - vértices relevantes que no sean el N_pre.

    Se mantiene simple y robusto: el centroide de los otros dos vértices
    decide por defecto. Los vértices individuales quedan como diagnóstico
    o como criterio opcional agresivo.
    """
    nodes = tri.get("nodes", [])

    other_nodes = [
        n for n in nodes
        if str(n.get("label", "")) != str(npre_node.get("label", ""))
    ]

    if not other_nodes:
        return None, []

    pts = np.array(
        [[float(n["x"]), float(n["y"])] for n in other_nodes],
        dtype=float
    )

    centroid_xy = np.mean(pts, axis=0)

    vertex_records = []

    for n in other_nodes:
        vertex_records.append({
            "label": str(n.get("label", "")),
            "node": n,
            "xy": node_xy_filter_9(n),
        })

    return centroid_xy, vertex_records


def evaluate_triangle_npre_laterality_filter_9(
    tri,
    npre_context_by_label,
    side_tol=1e-7
):
    """
    Evalúa lateralidad para todos los N_pre que aparezcan en un triángulo.

    Versión corregida:
      - Si un N_pre tiene varios generadores válidos, el triángulo se conserva
        si cae del lado válido de al menos uno de ellos.
      - Solo se elimina si queda del lado contrario a todos los generadores.
    """
    tri_ext = decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)
    labels = triangle_labels_filter_9(tri_ext)
    labels_fmt = format_labels_filter_9(labels)

    npre_nodes = [
        n for n in tri_ext.get("nodes", [])
        if is_npre_node_filter_9(n)
    ]

    if not ENABLE_NPRE_LATERALITY_FILTER_9 or not npre_nodes:
        return {
            "triangle_labels": labels,
            "triangle_labels_fmt": labels_fmt,
            "has_npre": bool(npre_nodes),
            "is_valid_lateral": True,
            "remove_by_lateral": False,
            "reason": "Sin N_pre o filtro lateral desactivado.",
            "npre_reports": [],
        }

    npre_reports = []
    invalid_reports = []

    for n_node in npre_nodes:
        n_label = str(n_node.get("label", ""))

        ctx = npre_context_by_label.get(n_label, None)

        if ctx is None:
            report = {
                "n_label": n_label,
                "status": "no_context_keep_by_safety",
                "can_apply": False,
                "is_valid_for_this_npre": True,
                "remove_by_this_npre": False,
                "reason": "No existe contexto de lateralidad para este N_pre.",
            }
            npre_reports.append(report)
            continue

        if not ctx.get("can_apply", False):
            report = {
                "n_label": n_label,
                "status": ctx.get("status", "unknown"),
                "can_apply": False,
                "is_valid_for_this_npre": True,
                "remove_by_this_npre": False,
                "reason": ctx.get("reason", "No se aplica lateralidad por seguridad."),
            }
            npre_reports.append(report)
            continue

        host_guard = ctx["host_guard"]
        valid_side_records = ctx.get("valid_side_records", [])

        if not valid_side_records:
            report = {
                "n_label": n_label,
                "status": "no_valid_side_records_keep_by_safety",
                "can_apply": True,
                "is_valid_for_this_npre": True,
                "remove_by_this_npre": False,
                "reason": "No hay lados válidos registrados para este N_pre.",
            }
            npre_reports.append(report)
            continue

        generator_labels = [
            rec.get("generator_label", "?")
            for rec in valid_side_records
        ]

        n_xy = node_xy_filter_9(n_node)
        v_guard = np.asarray(host_guard["v_xy"], dtype=float)

        centroid_xy, vertex_records = relevant_test_points_for_npre_triangle_filter_9(
            tri=tri_ext,
            npre_node=n_node,
            host_guard=host_guard
        )

        if centroid_xy is None:
            report = {
                "n_label": n_label,
                "status": "no_test_points_keep_by_safety",
                "can_apply": True,
                "is_valid_for_this_npre": True,
                "remove_by_this_npre": False,
                "reason": "No hay puntos de prueba para evaluar lateralidad.",
            }
            npre_reports.append(report)
            continue

        side_centroid = cross2d_filter_9(v_guard, centroid_xy - n_xy)

        centroid_compat_records = []

        for side_rec in valid_side_records:
            side_valid = float(side_rec["side_valid"])
            side_product = side_valid * side_centroid
            compatible = side_product >= -side_tol

            centroid_compat_records.append({
                "generator_label": side_rec.get("generator_label"),
                "side_valid": side_valid,
                "side_sign": int(side_rec.get("side_sign", 0)),
                "side_product_centroid": float(side_product),
                "compatible": bool(compatible),
            })

        centroid_accepted_by = [
            rec["generator_label"]
            for rec in centroid_compat_records
            if rec["compatible"]
        ]

        centroid_on_wrong_side = len(centroid_accepted_by) == 0

        vertex_side_reports = []
        any_vertex_wrong = False
        wrong_vertex_labels = []

        for vrec in vertex_records:
            side_vertex = cross2d_filter_9(v_guard, vrec["xy"] - n_xy)

            compat_records_vertex = []

            for side_rec in valid_side_records:
                side_valid = float(side_rec["side_valid"])
                side_product = side_valid * side_vertex
                compatible = side_product >= -side_tol

                compat_records_vertex.append({
                    "generator_label": side_rec.get("generator_label"),
                    "side_valid": side_valid,
                    "side_product": float(side_product),
                    "compatible": bool(compatible),
                })

            accepted_by_vertex = [
                rec["generator_label"]
                for rec in compat_records_vertex
                if rec["compatible"]
            ]

            wrong = len(accepted_by_vertex) == 0

            if wrong:
                any_vertex_wrong = True
                wrong_vertex_labels.append(vrec["label"])

            vertex_side_reports.append({
                "label": vrec["label"],
                "side_value": float(side_vertex),
                "wrong_side": bool(wrong),
                "accepted_by_generator_labels": accepted_by_vertex,
                "compatibility_records": compat_records_vertex,
            })

        remove_by_centroid = (
            NPRE_REMOVE_IF_CENTROID_WRONG_SIDE_9
            and centroid_on_wrong_side
        )

        remove_by_any_vertex = (
            NPRE_REMOVE_IF_ANY_VERTEX_WRONG_SIDE_9
            and any_vertex_wrong
        )

        remove_by_this_npre = bool(remove_by_centroid or remove_by_any_vertex)

        if remove_by_this_npre:
            reason = (
                f"Triángulo usa {n_label} fuera de todos sus dominios laterales válidos. "
                f"Generadores válidos={generator_labels}. "
                f"centroid_wrong={centroid_on_wrong_side}, "
                f"any_vertex_wrong={any_vertex_wrong}."
            )
        else:
            reason = (
                f"Triángulo compatible con lateralidad de {n_label}. "
                f"Aceptado por generador(es)={centroid_accepted_by}. "
                f"Generadores válidos={generator_labels}."
            )

        report = {
            "n_label": n_label,
            "status": "evaluated",
            "can_apply": True,
            "is_valid_for_this_npre": not remove_by_this_npre,
            "remove_by_this_npre": remove_by_this_npre,
            "reason": reason,
            "generator_labels": generator_labels,
            "accepted_by_generator_labels": centroid_accepted_by,
            "host_guard_labels": host_guard["labels"],
            "host_guard_idx": host_guard["guard_idx"],
            "valid_side_records": valid_side_records,
            "side_centroid": float(side_centroid),
            "centroid_on_wrong_side": bool(centroid_on_wrong_side),
            "centroid_compatibility_records": centroid_compat_records,
            "any_vertex_wrong_side": bool(any_vertex_wrong),
            "wrong_vertex_labels": wrong_vertex_labels,
            "vertex_side_reports": vertex_side_reports,

            # Campos de compatibilidad con la versión anterior.
            "generator_label": generator_labels[0] if generator_labels else None,
            "side_valid": float(valid_side_records[0]["side_valid"]),
            "side_sign": int(valid_side_records[0]["side_sign"]),
            "side_product_centroid": float(centroid_compat_records[0]["side_product_centroid"]),
        }

        npre_reports.append(report)

        if remove_by_this_npre:
            invalid_reports.append(report)

    remove_by_lateral = len(invalid_reports) > 0

    return {
        "triangle_labels": labels,
        "triangle_labels_fmt": labels_fmt,
        "has_npre": True,
        "is_valid_lateral": not remove_by_lateral,
        "remove_by_lateral": bool(remove_by_lateral),
        "reason": (
            "Triángulo eliminado por lateralidad N_pre."
            if remove_by_lateral
            else "Triángulo válido por lateralidad N_pre."
        ),
        "npre_reports": npre_reports,
        "invalid_reports": invalid_reports,
    }



# =========================================================
# 5B) LIMPIEZA FINAL N-N-M POR MISMA BASE N-N
# =========================================================

def signed_polygon_area_xy_filter_9(points_xy):
    """
    Área firmada de un polígono XY.
    Positiva si está en sentido antihorario.
    """
    pts = np.asarray(points_xy, dtype=float)

    if len(pts) < 3:
        return 0.0

    x = pts[:, 0]
    y = pts[:, 1]
    return 0.5 * float(np.dot(x, np.roll(y, -1)) - np.dot(y, np.roll(x, -1)))


def polygon_area_xy_filter_9(points_xy):
    """
    Área absoluta de un polígono XY.
    """
    return abs(signed_polygon_area_xy_filter_9(points_xy))


def triangle_points_xy_filter_9(tri):
    """
    Devuelve los tres puntos XY de un triángulo.
    """
    tri_ext = decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)
    return np.array(
        [[float(n["x"]), float(n["y"])] for n in tri_ext.get("nodes", [])],
        dtype=float
    )


def triangle_area_xy_filter_9(tri):
    """
    Área proyectada en planta XY de un triángulo.
    """
    pts = triangle_points_xy_filter_9(tri)

    if len(pts) != 3:
        return 0.0

    return polygon_area_xy_filter_9(pts)


def line_intersection_xy_filter_9(p1, p2, q1, q2, tol=1e-12):
    """
    Intersección de dos rectas 2D definidas por p1-p2 y q1-q2.
    Se usa dentro del recorte convexo de polígonos.
    """
    p1 = np.asarray(p1, dtype=float)
    p2 = np.asarray(p2, dtype=float)
    q1 = np.asarray(q1, dtype=float)
    q2 = np.asarray(q2, dtype=float)

    r = p2 - p1
    s = q2 - q1
    denom = cross2d_filter_9(r, s)

    if abs(denom) <= tol:
        return p2.copy()

    t = cross2d_filter_9(q1 - p1, s) / denom
    return p1 + t * r


def clip_polygon_by_convex_polygon_xy_filter_9(subject_polygon, clip_polygon, tol=1e-9):
    """
    Recorta un polígono convexo contra otro polígono convexo en XY usando
    Sutherland-Hodgman. Para este filtro se usa con triángulos.
    """
    subject = [np.asarray(p, dtype=float) for p in subject_polygon]
    clip = [np.asarray(p, dtype=float) for p in clip_polygon]

    if len(subject) < 3 or len(clip) < 3:
        return []

    clip_area_signed = signed_polygon_area_xy_filter_9(clip)

    if abs(clip_area_signed) <= tol:
        return []

    clip_is_ccw = clip_area_signed > 0.0

    def inside(p, a, b):
        val = cross2d_filter_9(b - a, p - a)
        if clip_is_ccw:
            return val >= -tol
        return val <= tol

    output = subject

    for i in range(len(clip)):
        a = clip[i]
        b = clip[(i + 1) % len(clip)]

        input_list = output
        output = []

        if not input_list:
            break

        s = input_list[-1]

        for e in input_list:
            e_inside = inside(e, a, b)
            s_inside = inside(s, a, b)

            if e_inside:
                if not s_inside:
                    output.append(line_intersection_xy_filter_9(s, e, a, b))
                output.append(e)
            elif s_inside:
                output.append(line_intersection_xy_filter_9(s, e, a, b))

            s = e

    return output


def triangle_intersection_area_xy_filter_9(tri_a, tri_b, tol=1e-9):
    """
    Calcula el área de intersección XY entre dos triángulos.
    Si el recorte falla o es degenerado, retorna 0.
    """
    pts_a = triangle_points_xy_filter_9(tri_a)
    pts_b = triangle_points_xy_filter_9(tri_b)

    if len(pts_a) != 3 or len(pts_b) != 3:
        return 0.0

    inter_poly = clip_polygon_by_convex_polygon_xy_filter_9(
        subject_polygon=pts_a,
        clip_polygon=pts_b,
        tol=tol
    )

    if len(inter_poly) < 3:
        return 0.0

    return polygon_area_xy_filter_9(inter_poly)


def get_nnm_base_and_mast_filter_9(tri):
    """
    Para un N-N-M devuelve:
      - base_key: labels ordenados de los dos N;
      - n_labels: labels de N;
      - mast_label: label del M;
      - n_nodes: nodos N;
      - mast_node: nodo M.
    """
    tri_ext = decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)

    if tri_ext.get("triangle_type") != "N-N-M":
        return None

    n_nodes = []
    m_nodes = []

    for n in tri_ext.get("nodes", []):
        fam = node_family_filter_9(n)
        if fam == "N":
            n_nodes.append(n)
        elif fam == "M":
            m_nodes.append(n)

    if len(n_nodes) != 2 or len(m_nodes) != 1:
        return None

    n_labels = [str(n.get("label", "")) for n in n_nodes]
    mast_label = str(m_nodes[0].get("label", ""))
    base_key = tuple(sorted(n_labels))

    return {
        "base_key": base_key,
        "n_labels": tuple(n_labels),
        "mast_label": mast_label,
        "n_nodes": n_nodes,
        "mast_node": m_nodes[0],
    }


def nnm_side_sign_against_base_filter_9(n_nodes, mast_node, side_tol=1e-7):
    """
    Calcula el lado del mástil M respecto a la línea N-N.
    """
    a_xy = node_xy_filter_9(n_nodes[0])
    b_xy = node_xy_filter_9(n_nodes[1])
    m_xy = node_xy_filter_9(mast_node)

    side_value = cross2d_filter_9(b_xy - a_xy, m_xy - a_xy)

    if abs(side_value) <= side_tol:
        side_sign = 0
    elif side_value > 0:
        side_sign = 1
    else:
        side_sign = -1

    return side_sign, float(side_value)


def get_mmn_records_for_nnm_cleanup_filter_9(triangles):
    """
    Extrae registros M-M-N para estimar qué N-N-M tiene más soporte o
    complemento de relleno posterior.
    """
    records = []

    for tri in triangles:
        tri_ext = decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)

        if tri_ext.get("triangle_type") != "M-M-N":
            continue

        m_labels = []
        n_labels = []

        for node in tri_ext.get("nodes", []):
            fam = node_family_filter_9(node)
            label = str(node.get("label", ""))

            if fam == "M":
                m_labels.append(label)
            elif fam == "N":
                n_labels.append(label)

        if len(m_labels) == 2 and len(n_labels) == 1:
            records.append({
                "triangle": tri_ext,
                "m_labels": tuple(sorted(m_labels)),
                "n_label": n_labels[0],
                "labels_fmt": format_labels_filter_9(triangle_labels_filter_9(tri_ext)),
            })

    return records


def complementary_mmn_count_for_nnm_filter_9(record, component_records, mmn_records):
    """
    Cuenta cuántos M-M-N complementarios existen para un N-N-M candidato.

    Para un N-N-M con base N1-N2 y mástil Mx, se consideran complementarios
    los M-M-N que:
      - contienen Mx;
      - contienen otro mástil My que también aparece en el grupo conflictivo;
      - contienen uno de los N de la base N1-N2.
    """
    base_n_set = set(record.get("base_key", ()))
    mast_label = record.get("mast_label")
    competing_masts = {
        r.get("mast_label")
        for r in component_records
        if r.get("mast_label") != mast_label
    }

    count = 0
    matched = []

    for mmn in mmn_records:
        mmn_m_set = set(mmn["m_labels"])
        mmn_n = mmn["n_label"]

        if mast_label not in mmn_m_set:
            continue

        if not (mmn_m_set & competing_masts):
            continue

        if mmn_n not in base_n_set:
            continue

        count += 1
        matched.append(mmn["labels_fmt"])

    return count, matched


def pair_nnm_same_base_conflict_filter_9(rec_a, rec_b):
    """
    Decide si dos N-N-M con la misma base N-N deben competir.

    Condiciones principales:
      - misma base N-N;
      - mismo lado de la base si NNM_SAME_NN_REQUIRE_SAME_SIDE_9=True;
      - áreas XY muy parecidas o solape XY significativo.
    """
    if rec_a["base_key"] != rec_b["base_key"]:
        return False, {
            "reason": "different_base",
            "is_conflict": False,
        }

    if NNM_SAME_NN_REQUIRE_SAME_SIDE_9:
        if rec_a["side_sign"] == 0 or rec_b["side_sign"] == 0:
            return False, {
                "reason": "mast_on_base_line_keep_by_safety",
                "is_conflict": False,
            }

        if rec_a["side_sign"] != rec_b["side_sign"]:
            return False, {
                "reason": "opposite_sides_of_NN_base",
                "is_conflict": False,
            }

    area_a = max(float(rec_a.get("area_xy", 0.0)), 0.0)
    area_b = max(float(rec_b.get("area_xy", 0.0)), 0.0)

    if area_a <= NNM_SAME_NN_POLYGON_TOL_9 or area_b <= NNM_SAME_NN_POLYGON_TOL_9:
        return False, {
            "reason": "degenerate_area_keep_by_safety",
            "is_conflict": False,
            "area_a": area_a,
            "area_b": area_b,
        }

    area_ratio = min(area_a, area_b) / max(area_a, area_b)
    similar_area = area_ratio >= (1.0 - NNM_SAME_NN_AREA_REL_TOL_9)

    overlap_area = 0.0
    overlap_ratio = 0.0
    overlap_conflict = False

    if NNM_SAME_NN_USE_OVERLAP_TEST_9:
        overlap_area = triangle_intersection_area_xy_filter_9(
            rec_a["triangle"],
            rec_b["triangle"],
            tol=NNM_SAME_NN_POLYGON_TOL_9
        )
        overlap_ratio = overlap_area / min(area_a, area_b)
        overlap_conflict = overlap_ratio >= NNM_SAME_NN_MIN_OVERLAP_RATIO_9

    is_conflict = bool(similar_area or overlap_conflict)

    if similar_area and overlap_conflict:
        reason = "same_base_same_side_similar_area_and_overlap"
    elif similar_area:
        reason = "same_base_same_side_similar_area"
    elif overlap_conflict:
        reason = "same_base_same_side_overlap"
    else:
        reason = "same_base_same_side_but_not_similar_enough"

    return is_conflict, {
        "reason": reason,
        "is_conflict": bool(is_conflict),
        "area_a": area_a,
        "area_b": area_b,
        "area_ratio": float(area_ratio),
        "similar_area": bool(similar_area),
        "overlap_area": float(overlap_area),
        "overlap_ratio": float(overlap_ratio),
        "overlap_conflict": bool(overlap_conflict),
    }


def connected_components_from_edges_filter_9(n_items, edges):
    """
    Componentes conectadas para agrupar N-N-M conflictivos.
    """
    parent = list(range(n_items))

    def find(x):
        while parent[x] != x:
            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]
            x = parent[x]
        return x

    def union(a, b):
        ra = find(a)
        rb = find(b)
        if ra != rb:
            parent[rb] = ra

    for a, b in edges:
        union(a, b)

    comps = {}
    for i in range(n_items):
        r = find(i)
        comps.setdefault(r, []).append(i)

    return list(comps.values())


def choose_nnm_winner_in_conflict_component_filter_9(component_records, mmn_records):
    """
    Selecciona el N-N-M ganador dentro de un conjunto conflictivo.
    """
    scored = []

    for rec in component_records:
        complement_count, complement_labels = complementary_mmn_count_for_nnm_filter_9(
            record=rec,
            component_records=component_records,
            mmn_records=mmn_records
        )

        eval_rec = rec["triangle"].get("nnm_guard_validation_9", {})
        valid_pair_count = len(eval_rec.get("valid_pairs", []))

        # Score determinístico:
        #   1) más M-M-N complementarios;
        #   2) más parejas estructurales válidas;
        #   3) primero en la lista de entrada.
        score = (
            int(complement_count),
            int(valid_pair_count),
            -int(rec["original_index"]),
        )

        scored.append({
            **rec,
            "score": score,
            "complementary_mmn_count": complement_count,
            "complementary_mmn_labels": complement_labels,
            "valid_pair_count": valid_pair_count,
        })

    scored.sort(key=lambda r: r["score"], reverse=True)
    return scored[0], scored


def cleanup_nnm_same_nn_overlap_filter_9(triangles):
    """
    Limpieza final de N-N-M conflictivos por misma base N-N.

    Entrada:
        - Lista de triángulos ya filtrados por la validación estructural N-N-M
          y por lateralidad N_pre.

    Salida:
        - kept_clean: triángulos conservados después de la limpieza.
        - kept_nnm_clean: N-N-M conservados después de la limpieza.
        - removed_nnm_same_nn: N-N-M removidos por conflicto de misma base N-N.
        - cleanup_log: diagnóstico detallado por grupos y pares.
    """
    if not ENABLE_NNM_SAME_NN_OVERLAP_CLEANUP_9:
        kept_nnm = [
            decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)
            for tri in triangles
            if decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri).get("triangle_type") == "N-N-M"
        ]

        return list(triangles), kept_nnm, [], [{
            "status": "disabled",
            "reason": "ENABLE_NNM_SAME_NN_OVERLAP_CLEANUP_9=False",
        }]

    records = []

    for idx, tri in enumerate(triangles):
        tri_ext = decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)

        if tri_ext.get("triangle_type") != "N-N-M":
            continue

        info = get_nnm_base_and_mast_filter_9(tri_ext)

        if info is None:
            continue

        side_sign, side_value = nnm_side_sign_against_base_filter_9(
            n_nodes=info["n_nodes"],
            mast_node=info["mast_node"],
            side_tol=NNM_SAME_NN_SIDE_TOL_9
        )

        area_xy = triangle_area_xy_filter_9(tri_ext)
        labels_fmt = format_labels_filter_9(triangle_labels_filter_9(tri_ext))

        records.append({
            "original_index": idx,
            "triangle": tri_ext,
            "labels": triangle_labels_filter_9(tri_ext),
            "labels_fmt": labels_fmt,
            "base_key": info["base_key"],
            "n_labels": info["n_labels"],
            "mast_label": info["mast_label"],
            "side_sign": side_sign,
            "side_value": side_value,
            "area_xy": area_xy,
        })

    # Si no hay suficientes N-N-M, no hay nada que limpiar.
    if len(records) <= 1:
        kept_nnm = [r["triangle"] for r in records]
        return list(triangles), kept_nnm, [], [{
            "status": "no_cleanup_needed",
            "reason": "Hay cero o un N-N-M después de las etapas previas.",
            "nnm_count": len(records),
        }]

    mmn_records = get_mmn_records_for_nnm_cleanup_filter_9(triangles)

    # Agrupar por misma base N-N y mismo lado.
    groups = {}

    for rec in records:
        if rec["side_sign"] == 0:
            # Si el M cae sobre la línea N-N, se conserva por seguridad y no compite.
            group_key = (rec["base_key"], "side_0_safety", rec["original_index"])
        elif NNM_SAME_NN_REQUIRE_SAME_SIDE_9:
            group_key = (rec["base_key"], rec["side_sign"])
        else:
            group_key = (rec["base_key"], "any_side")

        groups.setdefault(group_key, []).append(rec)

    removed_indices = set()
    removed_nnm_same_nn = []
    cleanup_log = []

    for group_key, group_records in groups.items():
        if len(group_records) <= 1:
            cleanup_log.append({
                "group_key": group_key,
                "status": "single_nnm_in_group_keep",
                "triangles": [r["labels_fmt"] for r in group_records],
            })
            continue

        conflict_edges = []
        pair_logs = []

        for i in range(len(group_records)):
            for j in range(i + 1, len(group_records)):
                is_conflict, pair_info = pair_nnm_same_base_conflict_filter_9(
                    group_records[i],
                    group_records[j]
                )

                pair_log = {
                    "triangle_a": group_records[i]["labels_fmt"],
                    "triangle_b": group_records[j]["labels_fmt"],
                    "mast_a": group_records[i]["mast_label"],
                    "mast_b": group_records[j]["mast_label"],
                    **pair_info,
                }
                pair_logs.append(pair_log)

                if is_conflict:
                    conflict_edges.append((i, j))

        if not conflict_edges:
            cleanup_log.append({
                "group_key": group_key,
                "status": "no_conflicts_in_group_keep_all",
                "triangles": [r["labels_fmt"] for r in group_records],
                "pair_logs": pair_logs,
            })
            continue

        components = connected_components_from_edges_filter_9(
            n_items=len(group_records),
            edges=conflict_edges
        )

        component_logs = []

        for comp in components:
            comp_records = [group_records[k] for k in comp]

            if len(comp_records) <= 1:
                component_logs.append({
                    "status": "component_without_conflict_keep",
                    "triangles": [r["labels_fmt"] for r in comp_records],
                })
                continue

            winner, scored_records = choose_nnm_winner_in_conflict_component_filter_9(
                component_records=comp_records,
                mmn_records=mmn_records
            )

            for rec in scored_records:
                if rec["original_index"] == winner["original_index"]:
                    continue

                tri_removed = dict(rec["triangle"])
                tri_removed["removed_reason"] = (
                    "N-N-M eliminado en limpieza final del Filtro 9 porque comparte "
                    "la misma base N-N con otro N-N-M del mismo lado y genera un "
                    "conflicto/solape local. Se conservó el candidato con mejor "
                    "soporte complementario M-M-N o, en empate, el primero de la lista."
                )
                tri_removed["removed_by_filter9_stage"] = "nnm_same_nn_overlap_cleanup"
                tri_removed["nnm_same_nn_cleanup_9"] = {
                    "base_key": rec["base_key"],
                    "side_sign": rec["side_sign"],
                    "area_xy": rec["area_xy"],
                    "winner_labels": winner["labels_fmt"],
                    "winner_mast_label": winner["mast_label"],
                    "candidate_score": rec.get("score"),
                    "winner_score": winner.get("score"),
                    "candidate_complementary_mmn_count": rec.get("complementary_mmn_count"),
                    "winner_complementary_mmn_count": winner.get("complementary_mmn_count"),
                }

                removed_indices.add(rec["original_index"])
                removed_nnm_same_nn.append(tri_removed)

            component_logs.append({
                "status": "conflict_component_resolved",
                "base_key": winner["base_key"],
                "side_sign": winner["side_sign"],
                "winner": winner["labels_fmt"],
                "winner_mast_label": winner["mast_label"],
                "winner_score": winner.get("score"),
                "candidates": [
                    {
                        "labels": rec["labels_fmt"],
                        "mast_label": rec["mast_label"],
                        "area_xy": rec["area_xy"],
                        "side_value": rec["side_value"],
                        "score": rec.get("score"),
                        "complementary_mmn_count": rec.get("complementary_mmn_count"),
                        "complementary_mmn_labels": rec.get("complementary_mmn_labels"),
                        "valid_pair_count": rec.get("valid_pair_count"),
                    }
                    for rec in scored_records
                ],
                "removed": [
                    rec["labels_fmt"]
                    for rec in scored_records
                    if rec["original_index"] != winner["original_index"]
                ],
            })

        cleanup_log.append({
            "group_key": group_key,
            "status": "processed_group",
            "triangles": [r["labels_fmt"] for r in group_records],
            "pair_logs": pair_logs,
            "component_logs": component_logs,
        })

    kept_clean = []

    for idx, tri in enumerate(triangles):
        if idx not in removed_indices:
            kept_clean.append(tri)

    kept_nnm_clean = [
        decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)
        for tri in kept_clean
        if decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri).get("triangle_type") == "N-N-M"
    ]

    return kept_clean, kept_nnm_clean, removed_nnm_same_nn, cleanup_log


# =========================================================
# 6) FILTRO PRINCIPAL
# =========================================================

def build_active_tri_nodes_after_filter_9(tri_nodes_input, triangles):
    """
    Conserva:
      - todos los mástiles M;
      - solo puntos Q/N que pertenezcan a triángulos conservados;
      - también agrega nodos que aparezcan en triángulos conservados
        aunque no estuvieran en tri_nodes_input.
    """
    node_by_label = {}

    for n in tri_nodes_input:
        node_by_label[str(n["label"])] = n

    for tri in triangles:
        for n in tri["nodes"]:
            node_by_label[str(n["label"])] = n

    active_labels = set()

    for tri in triangles:
        for n in tri["nodes"]:
            active_labels.add(str(n["label"]))

    active_nodes = []

    for label, n in node_by_label.items():
        if node_family_filter_9(n) == "M":
            active_nodes.append(n)
        elif label in active_labels:
            active_nodes.append(n)

    return active_nodes


def filter_nnm_and_npre_laterality_9(
    triangles,
    tri_nodes,
    masts,
    guard_wire_inputs=None,
    perp_dot_tol=0.087,
    cross_tol=1e-6,
    param_tol=1e-6,
    min_length=1e-9
):
    """
    Filtro principal combinado:

      1) Valida N-N-M por:
           - una arista perpendicular a 2 guardas;
           - otra arista distinta como segmento de guarda.

      2) Valida cualquier triángulo con N_pre por lateralidad:
           - el triángulo debe estar del lado del mástil generador/influenciador
             del N_pre.
    """
    guard_segments = guard_wire_segments_from_inputs_filter_9(
        masts=masts,
        guard_wire_inputs=guard_wire_inputs
    )

    npre_context_by_label = build_npre_lateral_context_filter_9(
        tri_nodes=tri_nodes,
        triangles=triangles,
        masts=masts,
        guard_segments=guard_segments
    )

    kept = []
    removed_nnm_structural = []
    removed_npre_lateral = []
    kept_nnm = []

    nnm_validation_log = []
    npre_lateral_log = []

    for tri in triangles:
        tri_ext = decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)
        tri_type = tri_ext["triangle_type"]

        # -------------------------------------------------
        # 1) Validación estructural N-N-M.
        # -------------------------------------------------
        if tri_type == "N-N-M":
            eval_rec = evaluate_nnm_guard_conditions_filter_9(
                tri_data=tri_ext,
                guard_segments=guard_segments,
                perp_dot_tol=perp_dot_tol,
                cross_tol=cross_tol,
                param_tol=param_tol,
                min_length=min_length
            )

            nnm_validation_log.append(eval_rec)
            tri_ext["nnm_guard_validation_9"] = eval_rec

            if not eval_rec["is_valid_nnm"]:
                tri_ext["removed_reason"] = (
                    "N-N-M eliminado porque no cumple simultáneamente: "
                    "una arista perpendicular a 2 guardas y otra arista "
                    "distinta como segmento de guarda."
                )
                tri_ext["removed_by_filter9_stage"] = "nnm_guard_structure"
                removed_nnm_structural.append(tri_ext)
                continue

            tri_ext["kept_reason_filter9_nnm_structure"] = (
                "N-N-M pasa criterio estructural: tiene una arista "
                "perpendicular a 2 guardas y otra arista distinta que es "
                "segmento de guarda."
            )

        else:
            tri_ext["kept_reason_filter9_nnm_structure"] = (
                f"{tri_type} no evaluado por criterio N-N-M; pasa a validación lateral N_pre."
            )

        # -------------------------------------------------
        # 2) Validación lateral N_pre.
        # -------------------------------------------------
        lateral_eval = evaluate_triangle_npre_laterality_filter_9(
            tri=tri_ext,
            npre_context_by_label=npre_context_by_label,
            side_tol=NPRE_LATERAL_SIDE_TOL_9
        )

        tri_ext["npre_lateral_validation_9"] = lateral_eval

        if lateral_eval.get("has_npre", False):
            npre_lateral_log.append(lateral_eval)

        if lateral_eval.get("remove_by_lateral", False):
            tri_ext["removed_reason"] = lateral_eval.get(
                "reason",
                "Triángulo eliminado por lateralidad N_pre."
            )
            tri_ext["removed_by_filter9_stage"] = "npre_laterality"
            removed_npre_lateral.append(tri_ext)
            continue

        # -------------------------------------------------
        # 3) Conservación final.
        # -------------------------------------------------
        tri_ext["kept_reason_filter9"] = (
            "Triángulo conservado después del criterio estructural N-N-M "
            "y la validación lateral N_pre."
        )

        kept.append(tri_ext)

        if tri_type == "N-N-M":
            kept_nnm.append(tri_ext)

    # -------------------------------------------------
    # 4) Limpieza final de N-N-M conflictivos por misma base N-N.
    # -------------------------------------------------
    (
        kept,
        kept_nnm,
        removed_nnm_same_nn_overlap,
        nnm_same_nn_overlap_cleanup_log,
    ) = cleanup_nnm_same_nn_overlap_filter_9(
        triangles=kept
    )

    tri_nodes_after = build_active_tri_nodes_after_filter_9(
        tri_nodes_input=tri_nodes,
        triangles=kept
    )

    removed_nnm_lateral = [
        tri for tri in removed_npre_lateral
        if decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)["triangle_type"] == "N-N-M"
    ]

    removed_nnm_all = (
        list(removed_nnm_structural)
        + list(removed_nnm_lateral)
        + list(removed_nnm_same_nn_overlap)
    )

    return (
        kept,
        kept_nnm,
        removed_nnm_all,
        removed_nnm_structural,
        removed_npre_lateral,
        tri_nodes_after,
        nnm_validation_log,
        npre_lateral_log,
        npre_context_by_label,
        guard_segments,
        removed_nnm_same_nn_overlap,
        nnm_same_nn_overlap_cleanup_log,
    )


# =========================================================
# 7) GRÁFICA
# =========================================================

def triangle_color_filter_9(tri_type):
    """
    Colores consistentes con los filtros anteriores.
    """
    tri_type = normalize_triangle_type_filter_9(tri_type)

    if tri_type == "M-M-M":
        return "gray"

    if tri_type == "M-M-Q":
        return "red"

    if tri_type == "N-N-M":
        return "green"

    if tri_type == "M-M-N":
        return "purple"

    return "black"


def triangle_width_filter_9(tri_type):
    """
    Todas las aristas de triángulos se dibujan con grosor 3.
    """
    return TRIANGLE_LINE_WIDTH_9


def plot_guard_segments_filter_9(fig, guard_segments):
    """
    Dibuja cables de guarda agrupados en una sola traza.
    """
    if not guard_segments:
        return

    x_vals = []
    y_vals = []
    z_vals = []
    text_vals = []

    for guard in guard_segments:
        p1 = guard["p1"]
        p2 = guard["p2"]

        hover_txt = f"Guarda {guard['label_a']} - {guard['label_b']}"

        x_vals.extend([p1[0], p2[0], None])
        y_vals.extend([p1[1], p2[1], None])
        z_vals.extend([p1[2], p2[2], None])
        text_vals.extend([hover_txt, hover_txt, None])

    fig.add_trace(go.Scatter3d(
        x=x_vals,
        y=y_vals,
        z=z_vals,
        mode="lines",
        line=dict(color="darkgreen", width=GUARD_LINE_WIDTH_9),
        name="Guardas",
        hoverinfo="text",
        text=text_vals,
        showlegend=True
    ))


def add_triangle_edges_grouped_by_type_filter_9(fig, triangles):
    """
    Dibuja aristas reales de triángulos agrupadas por tipo.
    La leyenda interactiva controla las líneas reales.
    """
    type_order = ["M-M-M", "M-M-Q", "N-N-M", "M-M-N"]

    grouped_edges = {
        tri_type: {
            "x": [],
            "y": [],
            "z": [],
            "text": []
        }
        for tri_type in type_order
    }

    other_group = {
        "x": [],
        "y": [],
        "z": [],
        "text": []
    }

    ordered_triangles = []
    ordered_triangles.extend([
        tri for tri in triangles
        if decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)["triangle_type"] == "M-M-M"
    ])
    ordered_triangles.extend([
        tri for tri in triangles
        if decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)["triangle_type"] == "M-M-Q"
    ])
    ordered_triangles.extend([
        tri for tri in triangles
        if decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)["triangle_type"] == "M-M-N"
    ])
    ordered_triangles.extend([
        tri for tri in triangles
        if decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)["triangle_type"] == "N-N-M"
    ])
    ordered_triangles.extend([
        tri for tri in triangles
        if decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)["triangle_type"]
        not in ["M-M-M", "M-M-Q", "N-N-M", "M-M-N"]
    ])

    for tri_data in ordered_triangles:
        tri_ext = decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri_data)
        tri_type = tri_ext["triangle_type"]

        n1, n2, n3 = tri_ext["nodes"]
        labels = triangle_labels_filter_9(tri_ext)
        labels_fmt = format_labels_filter_9(labels)

        target_group = grouped_edges.get(tri_type, other_group)

        for a, b in [(n1, n2), (n2, n3), (n3, n1)]:
            target_group["x"].extend([a["x"], b["x"], None])
            target_group["y"].extend([a["y"], b["y"], None])
            target_group["z"].extend([a["z"], b["z"], None])

            hover_txt = (
                f"Tipo: {tri_type}<br>"
                f"Triángulo: {labels_fmt}<br>"
                f"Arista: {a.get('label', '')} - {b.get('label', '')}"
            )

            target_group["text"].extend([hover_txt, hover_txt, None])

    legend_names = {
        "M-M-M": "Triángulos MMM",
        "M-M-Q": "Triángulos MMQ",
        "N-N-M": "Triángulos NNM",
        "M-M-N": "Triángulos MMN",
    }

    for tri_type in type_order:
        data = grouped_edges[tri_type]

        if len(data["x"]) == 0:
            continue

        fig.add_trace(go.Scatter3d(
            x=data["x"],
            y=data["y"],
            z=data["z"],
            mode="lines",
            line=dict(
                color=triangle_color_filter_9(tri_type),
                width=triangle_width_filter_9(tri_type)
            ),
            name=legend_names.get(tri_type, tri_type),
            hoverinfo="text",
            text=data["text"],
            showlegend=True
        ))

    if len(other_group["x"]) > 0:
        fig.add_trace(go.Scatter3d(
            x=other_group["x"],
            y=other_group["y"],
            z=other_group["z"],
            mode="lines",
            line=dict(color="black", width=TRIANGLE_LINE_WIDTH_9),
            name="Otros triángulos",
            hoverinfo="text",
            text=other_group["text"],
            showlegend=True
        ))


def add_removed_triangles_grouped_filter_9(
    fig,
    removed_triangles,
    name,
    color,
    dash="dash"
):
    """
    Dibuja triángulos eliminados opcionalmente.
    """
    if not removed_triangles:
        return

    x_vals = []
    y_vals = []
    z_vals = []
    text_vals = []

    for tri_data in removed_triangles:
        tri_ext = decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri_data)
        n1, n2, n3 = tri_ext["nodes"]
        labels = triangle_labels_filter_9(tri_ext)
        labels_fmt = format_labels_filter_9(labels)

        xs = [n1["x"], n2["x"], n3["x"], n1["x"], None]
        ys = [n1["y"], n2["y"], n3["y"], n1["y"], None]
        zs = [n1["z"], n2["z"], n3["z"], n1["z"], None]

        hover_txt = (
            f"{name}<br>"
            f"{labels_fmt}<br>"
            f"Tipo={tri_ext.get('triangle_type')}<br>"
            f"{tri_ext.get('removed_reason', '')}"
        )

        x_vals.extend(xs)
        y_vals.extend(ys)
        z_vals.extend(zs)
        text_vals.extend([hover_txt for _ in xs])

    fig.add_trace(go.Scatter3d(
        x=x_vals,
        y=y_vals,
        z=z_vals,
        mode="lines",
        line=dict(color=color, width=TRIANGLE_LINE_WIDTH_9, dash=dash),
        name=name,
        hoverinfo="text",
        text=text_vals,
        showlegend=True
    ))


def add_validation_edges_filter_9(fig, kept_nnm):
    """
    Dibuja, opcionalmente, las aristas que validaron cada N-N-M:
      - perpendicular a 2 guardas;
      - segmento de guarda.
    """
    if not kept_nnm:
        return

    x_perp, y_perp, z_perp, text_perp = [], [], [], []
    x_guard, y_guard, z_guard, text_guard = [], [], [], []

    for tri in kept_nnm:
        tri_ext = decorate_triangle_type_filter_9(tri)
        edges = triangle_edges_filter_9(tri_ext)
        labels_fmt = format_labels_filter_9(triangle_labels_filter_9(tri_ext))
        eval_rec = tri_ext.get("nnm_guard_validation_9", {})

        perp_indices = set(eval_rec.get("perp_edge_indices", []))
        guard_indices = set(eval_rec.get("guard_segment_edge_indices", []))

        for edge_idx, (na, nb) in enumerate(edges):
            if edge_idx in perp_indices:
                x_perp.extend([na["x"], nb["x"], None])
                y_perp.extend([na["y"], nb["y"], None])
                z_perp.extend([na["z"], nb["z"], None])
                txt = f"NNM {labels_fmt}<br>Arista perpendicular a 2 guardas: {na.get('label')} - {nb.get('label')}"
                text_perp.extend([txt, txt, None])

            if edge_idx in guard_indices:
                x_guard.extend([na["x"], nb["x"], None])
                y_guard.extend([na["y"], nb["y"], None])
                z_guard.extend([na["z"], nb["z"], None])
                txt = f"NNM {labels_fmt}<br>Arista segmento de guarda: {na.get('label')} - {nb.get('label')}"
                text_guard.extend([txt, txt, None])

    if len(x_perp) > 0:
        fig.add_trace(go.Scatter3d(
            x=x_perp,
            y=y_perp,
            z=z_perp,
            mode="lines",
            line=dict(color="cyan", width=VALIDATION_SEGMENT_WIDTH_9),
            name="Aristas perpendiculares a 2 guardas",
            hoverinfo="text",
            text=text_perp,
            showlegend=True
        ))

    if len(x_guard) > 0:
        fig.add_trace(go.Scatter3d(
            x=x_guard,
            y=y_guard,
            z=z_guard,
            mode="lines",
            line=dict(color="lime", width=VALIDATION_SEGMENT_WIDTH_9),
            name="Aristas segmento de guarda",
            hoverinfo="text",
            text=text_guard,
            showlegend=True
        ))


def add_npre_validity_arrows_filter_9(fig, npre_context_by_label):
    """
    Dibuja flechas/líneas de referencia N_pre -> generador.
    Soporta múltiples generadores válidos por N_pre.
    """
    if not SHOW_NPRE_VALIDITY_ARROWS_9:
        return

    x_vals = []
    y_vals = []
    z_vals = []
    text_vals = []

    for n_label, ctx in npre_context_by_label.items():
        if not ctx.get("can_apply", False):
            continue

        n_node = ctx["n_node"]
        host = ctx["host_guard"]
        valid_side_records = ctx.get("valid_side_records", [])

        if not valid_side_records:
            # Compatibilidad con versión anterior.
            if "generator_node" in ctx:
                valid_side_records = [ctx]
            else:
                continue

        for rec in valid_side_records:
            g_node = rec.get("generator_node", None)

            if g_node is None:
                continue

            txt = (
                f"Lateralidad {n_label}<br>"
                f"Generador: {rec.get('generator_label')}<br>"
                f"Host: {host.get('labels')}<br>"
                f"side_valid={rec.get('side_valid'):.6g}<br>"
                f"source={rec.get('source')}"
            )

            x_vals.extend([n_node["x"], g_node["x"], None])
            y_vals.extend([n_node["y"], g_node["y"], None])
            z_vals.extend([n_node["z"], g_node["z"], None])
            text_vals.extend([txt, txt, None])

    if len(x_vals) == 0:
        return

    fig.add_trace(go.Scatter3d(
        x=x_vals,
        y=y_vals,
        z=z_vals,
        mode="lines",
        line=dict(color="orange", width=5, dash="dot"),
        name="Dirección válida N_pre → generador(es)",
        hoverinfo="text",
        text=text_vals,
        showlegend=True
    ))


